Run records of codegen/c/compare_test.go's tests that build a program with clang flags
of their own and run it, written by tackc's porttest/rungen and completed
by tools/corpus --update; see tools/corpus/runs.tck for the format.
-- mixed-compare-example-is-sanitizer-clean/record --
replaces codegen/c/compare_test.go TestMixedCompareExampleIsSanitizerClean/-O0
replaces codegen/c/compare_test.go TestMixedCompareExampleIsSanitizerClean/-O1
strict-libs the test compiles its build's C with -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 at its level and flags itself, which the driver's -w turns off; the runner compiles it so
dir examples/mixed-compare
opt 0 1
cflags -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 -fsanitize=address,undefined -fsanitize-address-use-after-return=always -fno-sanitize-recover=all -fno-sanitize-address-globals-dead-stripping -ffinite-loops -mllvm -indvars-predicate-loops=true
lacks stdout "FAIL"
count stdout 8 " ok\n"
exit 0
stdout "int64 and uint64 ok\n"
stdout "narrow pairs ok\n"
stdout "target widths ok\n"
stdout "known values ok\n"
stdout "evaluation order ok\n"
stdout "guard on len ok\n"
stdout "facts ok\n"
stdout "switches ok\n"
stderr ""
